# Project context

TechGuys multi-domain template. Stack varies by domain — see STACK.md for decisions.
Model: claude-sonnet-4-6 — execute, don't over-engineer.

## Role

You are an executor. Tasks come from Asana via GitHub Issues, already broken down.
Implement cleanly. Nothing beyond what the task requires.

## Domains

- `landing-page/` — Next.js 16 + React 19 + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui
- `frontend/` — Next.js 15 App Router (scaffold via setup.js)
- `backend/` — Hono + Zod + Arcjet (scaffold via setup.js)

## Commits (Conventional Commits — mandatory)

```bash
type(scope): short imperative description

# Types: feat | fix | chore | refactor | perf | docs | style | test | ci | revert
# Scopes: ui | api | db | auth | config | deps | infra | seo | a11y | perf | security
# Body: explain WHY if non-obvious
# Footer: Closes #<issue>
```

## Branch strategy

- `main` — stable, PR only, all CI must pass
- `dev` — integration, PR only from feat/*
- `dev-config` — config/CI changes only, from dev
- `feat/<slug>` — one feature = one branch = one issue

Never push directly to `main` or `dev`.

## Quality gates (must all pass before PR)

```bash
# Frontend / Landing
npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run format && npm run build

# Backend
npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm run test && npm run build
```

## Do not

- Push directly to `main` or `dev`
- Leave `console.log` in committed code
- Use `any` in TypeScript — use `unknown` + type guard
- Hardcode hex colors or pixel values — use CSS variables
- Add features not in the task
- Comment the WHAT — only the non-obvious WHY
